From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: ath11k: nss: do not arm WDS backhaul on a plain AP

Every AP vdev unconditionally arms WDS backhaul mode in the wifili
firmware, regardless of whether any WDS or 4-address peer exists. The
firmware then keeps WDS/AST state for every peer and reports it back
through NSS_WIFILI_WDS_ACTIVE_INFO_MSG - a message this driver has no
handler for at all.

Measured on GL-B3000 (IPQ5018, firmware NSS.FW.12.2-156-MP.R): the
firmware emits that notification 2 ms after the VAP self peer is
created (err field 0x800) and again 244 ms after a station peer is
created, this time carrying 0x4b4b0800 - the upper half being the
usual poison pattern - and then stops servicing every queue, taking
the ethernet acceleration down with it.

DEBUG ONLY - the proper fix is to arm the mode only when a WDS peer
is actually configured, and to handle the firmware's WDS events.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -1529,12 +1529,24 @@
 		if (ret)
 			goto unregister_vdev;
 
-		ret = ath11k_nss_vdev_set_cmd(arvif,
-					      ATH11K_NSS_WIFI_VDEV_CFG_WDS_BACKHAUL_CMD,
-					      true);
-		if (ret) {
-			ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to cfg wds backhaul in nss %d\n", ret);
-			goto unregister_vdev;
+		/* DEBUG E63: this used to arm WDS backhaul mode on every AP,
+		 * whether or not any WDS/4-address peer exists. The firmware
+		 * then runs its WDS/AST bookkeeping for each new peer and
+		 * notifies the host through NSS_WIFILI_WDS_ACTIVE_INFO_MSG,
+		 * which this driver does not handle at all - there is no case
+		 * for it in the event handler. Measured on IPQ5018: the
+		 * firmware sends that notification a fraction of a second
+		 * after a station peer is created, with a poisoned payload
+		 * (0x4b4b0800), and stops executing immediately afterwards.
+		 */
+		if (0) {
+			ret = ath11k_nss_vdev_set_cmd(arvif,
+						      ATH11K_NSS_WIFI_VDEV_CFG_WDS_BACKHAUL_CMD,
+						      true);
+			if (ret) {
+				ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to cfg wds backhaul in nss %d\n", ret);
+				goto unregister_vdev;
+			}
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
